{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"e21d81da25c9311c6cb2e1baa20bbd18fe9e4a31eaa8e390fd029fa0a5d367e8","packTokens":1893,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":206,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":843,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":737,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"Map each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Build every operation of the locked API contract in contracts/openapi.yaml, exactly as it is written there.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Keep the data in the project's PostgreSQL database (the connection string named App, which the project already reads).\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Write sample data in App.Api/SeedData.cs: a few believable rows for each table, taken from the contract's examples, so each list has something to show.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"No test may count on those rows, because the app runs that file only when the setting Seed:Demo is true.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Do not build screens here; the web app is built in its own repo.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"Should authentication and authorization be enforced only where contracts/openapi.yaml explicitly requires them, or should additional access rules be added?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Enforce only authentication/authorization requirements explicitly declared by contracts/openapi.yaml; do not add extra role rules.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"What should happen for paths or HTTP methods that are not defined in the contract?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use normal 404/405 responses and add no undocumented operations.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"If demo seed data cannot be written to PostgreSQL when Seed:Demo is true, how should startup behave?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Fail startup and surface the seed-write error.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"Should successful API writes remain available after the API process restarts?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use normal PostgreSQL durability so successful writes remain available after an API restart.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Approve all 13 requirements in one run.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"Should all 13 requirements be approved as one run, or should the work be split by cutting or deferring a part?\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Apply only the lot-list filtering and security rules declared in contracts/openapi.yaml; add no authorizedYards restriction.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Should lot-list responses apply an additional authorizedYards restriction beyond the filtering and security rules declared in the API contract?\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Add separate cases for the contract-defined view-only and export-only paths, checking their respective redaction and export-denial behavior.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"How should the profitability permission checks be covered for users with view and export permissions independently?\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Calculate stock using opening stock and all persisted receipts, adjustments, and feeding events, incorporating the correction or void.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"After correcting or voiding a feeding event, how should the resulting stock be calculated when other persisted movements affect the same items?\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-9\",\n  \"question\": \"What must AC-10.2 verify after a confirmed sample reset or replacement?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Verify the affected sample records were actually removed by reset or replaced by the replacement sample records, in addition to checking completion and recordCount.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-10\",\n  \"question\": \"What should the sign-in acceptance criteria cover for incorrect credentials sent to POST /auth/sign-in?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Add one case confirming incorrect credentials receive the contract-defined rejection response.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Implement the Feedlot API exactly as declared in the OpenAPI contract: all documented operations, schemas, status codes, and security rules; no undocumented operations or product-screen routes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Return contract-defined sign-in, session, dashboard, and filtered lot-list responses, without applying an extra authorized-yard restriction to lot-list results.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Implement procurement imports and allocations with the contract-defined matching, PO-line-to-lot and lot-to-pen traceability, saved quantities, capacity information, and conflict results.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Implement lot forecasts, forecast settings, metrics, insights, planner actions, and weight-history operations with contract-defined calculations, suggestions, validation, and persisted updates.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Implement inventory reads, item writes, movements, projections, and CSV exports with contract-defined stock values and persist inventory changes in PostgreSQL.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Implement ration reads, creation, revision, optimization, and approval with contract-defined calculations and persisted changes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Implement feed-plan reads, creation, review, and status changes with contract-defined plan calculations, audit fields, and persisted updates.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Implement feeding-event reads, creation, correction, and voiding with contract-defined variance, cost, energy, inventory movements, and lot-feed totals; reconcile stock without counting replaced or voided movements.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Implement operational, feed-to-gain, and profitability reports and exports with contract-defined filters, calculations, authorization, and export artifacts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Implement sample-data status, load, reset, and replacement operations; avoid duplicate loading and require explicit confirmation for reset or replacement.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Store contract domain data in the configured App PostgreSQL database, preserve successful writes across restarts, and upgrade the schema without changing existing data.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"When Seed:Demo is true, seed each empty application table at startup with 3 to 5 believable, contract-example-derived rows, leave nonempty tables unchanged, and fail startup while surfacing seed-write errors.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"When Seed:Demo is false, serve collection operations from persisted records, including empty lists when no records exist.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}